### Background and motivation

Similar to https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/79868, but for [System.IO.FileAttributes](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.io.fileattributes?view=net-7.0&WT.mc_id=DT-MVP-5003978).

One use-case for the `0` value is when enumerating files. `0` allows to not exclude files from enumeration based on their attributes.

````
new System.IO.EnumerationOptions()
{
    AttributesToSkip = 0,
}
````

### API Proposal

```csharp
namespace System.IO;

[System.Flags]
public enum FileAttributes
{
    None = 0,

    // Existing values:
    // ReadOnly
    // Hidden
    // ...
```


### API Usage

```csharp
Directory.EnumerateFiles("folder", "*", new System.IO.EnumerationOptions()
{
    AttributesToSkip = FileAttributes.None,
});
```

Could also be used in https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/967250cc86b4c613015066b47b882e7424fdb590/src/libraries/System.Private.CoreLib/src/System/IO/Enumeration/FileSystemEnumerator.Unix.cs#L132

